L196: cite81†.github/workflows | cite81†.github/workflows |    |\nL197: cite82†assets | cite82†assets |    |\nL198: cite83†configs | cite83†configs |    |\nL199: cite84†data_toolkit | cite84†data_toolkit |    |\nL200: cite85†o-voxel | cite85†o-voxel |    |\nL201: cite86†trellis2 | cite86†trellis2 |    |\nL202: cite87†.gitignore | cite87†.gitignore |    |\nL203: cite88†.gitmodules | cite88†.gitmodules |    |\nL204: cite89†LICENSE | cite89†LICENSE |    |\nL205: cite90†README.md | cite90†README.md |    |\nL206: cite91†SECURITY.md | cite91†SECURITY.md |    |\nL207: cite92†app.py | cite92†app.py |    |\nL208: cite93†app_texturing.py | cite93†app_texturing.py |    |\nL209: cite94†example.py | cite94†example.py |    |\nL210: cite95†example_texturing.py | cite95†example_texturing.py |    |\nL211: cite96†setup.sh | cite96†setup.sh |    |\nL212: cite97†train.py | cite97†train.py |    |\nL213: [Button: View all files]\nL214: ## Repository files navigation\nL215: \nL216:   *   * cite98†README L217:   * cite98†Code of conduct L218:   * cite98†MIT license L219:   * cite98†Security L220: \nL221: More items\nL222: # Native and Compact Structured Latents for 3D Generation\nL223: \nL224: trellis2.mp4\nL225: \nL226: (Compressed version due to GitHub size limits. See the full-quality video on our project page!)\nL227: \nL228: TRELLIS.2 is a state-of-the-art large 3D generative model (4B parameters) designed for high-fidelity image-to-3D generation. It leverages a novel \"field-free\" sparse voxel structure termed O-Voxel to reconstruct and generate arbitrary 3D assets with complex topologies, sharp features, and full PBR materials.\nL229: \nL230: ## ✨ Features\nL231: ### 1. High Quality, Resolution & Efficiency\nL232: \nL233: Our 4B-parameter model generates high-resolution fully textured assets with exceptional fidelity and efficiency using vanilla DiTs. It utilizes a Sparse 3D VAE with 16× spatial downsampling to encode assets into a compact latent space.\nL234: \nL235: Resolution  | Total Time*  | Breakdown (Shape + Mat)\nL236: --- | --- | ---\nL237: 512³  | ~3s  | 2s + 1s\nL238: 1024³  | ~17s  | 10s + 7s\nL239: 1536³  | ~60s  | 35s + 25s\nL240: \nL241: *Tested on NVIDIA H100 GPU.\nL242: ### 2. Arbitrary Topology Handling\nL243: \nL244: The O-Voxel representation breaks the limits of iso-surface fields. It robustly handles complex structures without lossy conversion:\nL245: \nL246:   * ✅ Open Surfaces (e.g., clothing, leaves)\nL247:   * ✅ Non-manifold Geometry\nL248:   * ✅ Internal Enclosed Structures\nL249: \nL250: ### 3. Rich Texture Modeling\nL251: \nL252: Beyond basic colors, TRELLIS.2 models arbitrary surface attributes including Base Color, Roughness, Metallic, and Opacity, enabling photorealistic rendering and transparency support.\nL253: ### 4. Minimalist Processing\nL254: \nL255: Data processing is streamlined for instant conversions that are fully rendering-free and optimization-free.\nL256: \nL257:   * < 10s (Single CPU): Textured Mesh → O-Voxel\nL258:   * < 100ms (CUDA): O-Voxel → Textured Mesh\nL259: \nL260: ## 🗺️ Roadmap\nL261: \nL262:   * [Input] Paper release\nL263:   * [Input] Release image-to-3D inference code\nL264:   * [Input] Release pretrained checkpoints (4B)\nL265:   * [Input] Hugging Face Spaces demo\nL266:   * [Input] Release shape-conditioned texture generation inference code\nL267:   * [Input] Release training code\nL268: ## 🛠️ Installation\nL269: \nL270: ### Prerequisites\nL271: \nL272:   * System: The code is currently tested only on Linux.\nL273:   * Hardware: An NVIDIA GPU with at least 24GB of memory is necessary. The code has been verified on NVIDIA A100 and H100 GPUs.\nL274:   * Software:\nL275:     * The cite99†CUDA Toolkit†developer.nvidia.com is needed to compile certain packages. Recommended version is 12.4.\nL276:     * cite100†Conda†docs.anaconda.com is recommended for managing dependencies.\nL277:     * Python version 3.8 or higher is required.\nL278: ### Installation Steps\nL279: \nL280:   1. Clone the repo:\nL281: \nL282:     git clone -b main https://github.com/microsoft/TRELLIS.2.git --recursive\nL283:     cd TRELLIS.2\nL284: \nL285:   2. Install the dependencies:\nL286: \nL287: Before running the following command there are somethings to note:\nL288:      * By adding `--new-env`, a new conda environment named `trellis2` will be created. If you want to use an existing conda environment, please remove this flag.\nL289:      * By default the `trellis2` environment will use pytorch 2.6.0 with CUDA 12.4. If you want to use a different version of CUDA, you can remove the `--new-env` flag and manually install the required dependencies. Refer to cite101†PyTorch†pytorch.org for the installation command.\nL290:      * If you have multiple CUDA Toolkit versions installed, `CUDA_HOME` should be set to the correct version before running the command. For example, if you have CUDA Toolkit 12.4 and 13.0 installed, you can run `export CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-12.4` before running the command.\nL291:      * By default, the code uses the `flash-attn` backend for attention. For GPUs do not support `flash-attn` (e.g., NVIDIA V100), you can install `xformers` manually and set the `ATTN_BACKEND` environment variable to `xformers` before running the code. See the cite102†Minimal Example for more details.\nL292:      * The installation may take a while due to the large number of dependencies. Please be patient. If you encounter any issues, you can try to install the dependencies one by one, specifying one flag at a time.\nL293:      * If you encounter any issues during the installation, feel free to open an issue or contact us.\nL294: Create a new conda environment named `trellis2` and install the dependencies:\nL295: \nL296:     . ./setup.sh --new-env --basic --flash-attn --nvdiffrast --nvdiffrec --cumesh --o-voxel --flexgemm\nL297: The detailed usage of `setup.sh` can be found by running `. ./setup.sh --help`.\nL298: \nL299:     Usage: setup.sh [OPTIONS]\nL300:     Options:\nL301:         -h, --help              Display this help message\nL302:         --new-env               Create a new conda environment\nL303:         --basic                 Install basic dependencies\nL304:         --flash-attn            Install flash-attention\nL305:         --cumesh                Install cumesh\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModel Spec (2025/12/18) (https://model-spec.openai.com/2025-12-18.html)\nciteturn6476view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://model-spec.openai.com/2025-12-18.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 5127\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProtecting the wellbeing of our users \\ Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com/news/protecting-well-being-of-users)\nciteturn6476view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/protecting-well-being-of-users\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 97\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroducing Agent Skills | Claude by Anthropic (https://claude.com/resources/articles/skills)\nciteturn6476view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/skills\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 397\n"
